<title>SOUTH AFRICA: NEW S.AFRICAN BANKING GROUP MERGES FOUR OPERATIONS.</title>
<headline>NEW S.AFRICAN BANKING GROUP MERGES FOUR OPERATIONS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>A new banking group has been formed, merging Citizen Bank, Future Bank, Bophuthatswana Building Society and Msele Corporate and Merchant Bank, controlling shareholder Msele Financial Holdings said on Friday.</p>
<p>First National Bank will have a 25 percent stake in the venture which is to be headed by former BOE NatWest general manager Inus Prinsloo.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
